## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | lib/src/cli/approval_commands.dart | 🚨 blocking the sessions container walk gates boot — contradicts ac6 and reintroduces an unbounded fs wait on the startup path logbootline is awaited inside run agent cli dart 2159 and it awaits startsessionscontainergauge here approval commands dart 924 which awaits the full recursive walk of config sessionroot final stats await future at line 936 this contradicts the pr s own contract twice the function s own doc comment lines 927–930 starts the sessions container walk at boot unawaited — the walk must never gate boot the pr description ac6 a sessions container … line computed out of band so it never gates boot concretely sessionscontainersize lists every directory recursively and ioexecutionenv listdir io execution env dart 300 awaits a fileinfo stat per entry on the incident s 77 gb container this delays run boot before wiretransientretrynotice and everything after by a full cold cache stat walk on every start interactive and headless worse none of it is bounded — on a hung container fs the exact wedge shape this pr fixes listdir blocks forever with no timeout no named error and no banner boot itself now wedges which is strictly worse than the pre pr behavior and the intended design fix is one word dart future void logbootline async logdiagnostic fa boot sid logsid version version fds fdgaugelabel await openfdcount env fs fail 1m sessioniohealth failuresinlastminute unawaited startsessionscontainergauge stats already handles the not yet computed case sessions container not computed yet and the memoization keeps the boot line landing whenever the walk finishes no existing test pins the never gates boot invariant so this regressed silently — worth adding an assertion that run s boot sequence does not wait on containersizefuture |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/agent_cli_diag_log.dart | ⚠️ important the ac4 recovery flush is unbounded — an ok→hang fs wedges the whole diagnostic chain and the exit drain ac4 correctly bounds the live append lines 124–129 timeout config sessioniotimeout … but recoverdiagsink — which runs inside the serialized gh 2097 append chain appenddiagnosticlog → if iostate diagfailing await recoverdiagsink path — re appends the buffered ring and the recovery marker with no timeout dart for final bufferedline in buffered final landed await env appendfile path bufferedline ← unbounded … final marker await env appendfile path … ← unbounded trigger the sink fails once buffering starts one append then succeeds recovery fires and the next append hangs — the flaky fs shape intermittent mount fd pressure the acs target recoverdiagsink never returns diaglogchain wedges permanently every later logdiagnostic queues behind it and flushdiagnosticlog the exit drain awaited on every exit path — agent cli lifecycle dart 132 agent cli dart 2559 never completes the process cannot exit that is the same unbounded session io wait class this pr exists to eliminate surviving inside the new machinery bound each flush marker append the same way as the live append — on timeout treat it as a flush failure bufferdiagline line back into the ring keep diagfailing true instead of awaiting forever dart final landed await env appendfile path bufferedline timeout config sessioniotimeout ontimeout …err… the agent cli diag log sink test dart suite covers fail→recover and fail→exit but not fail→ok→hang a hanging flush case in wedgeenv would pin this contract |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/session/session_storage.dart | 💡 suggestion sessioniohealth also notes notfound failures — benign file missing arms the session io failing banner fsorthrow now notes every surfaced err into the per session io health before the error code mapping line 277 and the twin in windowed session storage dart 1297 — including fileerrorcode notfound which this same function maps to sessionerrorcode notfound precisely because it is not a storage health condition a genuinely missing path session deleted by retention user while a handle is open a raced exists → open is not an fs health signal yet it 1 arms ac5 s reclassification — the next stall banner reads ⚠ session io failing … restart the host check open fds container access even though the filesystem is healthy restart won t help — the levers ac5 set out to stop lying 2 inflates the fs op failures 1m gauge on stats and the boot line retrytransientsessionfileio already treats notfound as a non health transient the 427 reg test asserts a flaky append leaves sessioniohealth lastfailure null — exhaustion only surfacing so the storages are one condition away from consistency dart if sessionid null error code fileerrorcode notfound sessioniohealth notefailure sessionid text alternatively note it but with a distinct label so stallissessionio can ignore it the pr s border case list covers intermittence and per session isolation but not this case |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

